Z||000004||CountFiero||12-14-2001||05:27 PM||||Why would you WANT to "gut" the tank in the first place???  I don't understand the reason for wanting to remove baffles, if you aren't Filling the tank anyway.  Just a note of Warning.  You shouldn't run the car with the fuel that low all of the time.  It tends to "suck" the CRUD off of the bottom of the tank which will eventually cause the fuel filter to get clogged up.  Which in turn will make the car run poorly.  Gas isn't THAT expensive try keeping it FILLED -- especially in colder weather.  A partially filled tank will encourage the formation of condensation inside the tank which causes water to get into the fuel system.  Again this CAN be a MAJOR cause of cold weather problems---i.e. Frozen fuel lines.  If I was running on a 1/4 tank on a Regular basis I'd be adding a container of "HEET" from time to time to insure that the water in the system got evaporated.||||reg||1
